      <h3>3.6 Vulnerability Management</h3>
      <p>Every software system contains vulnerabilities — bugs and weaknesses that attackers can exploit. AI-powered
        vulnerability scanners continuously probe networks, prioritise vulnerabilities by composite risk score
        (exploitability × asset criticality × public exposure), and recommend patches — ensuring the most dangerous gaps
        are closed first rather than following an arbitrary queue.</p>

      <h3>3.7 Fraud Detection in Financial Cybercrime</h3>
      <p>Banks and payment processors use AI to analyse every transaction in real-time. Features like transaction
        amount, time, merchant category, geographic location, and the user's historical patterns are fed into ML models
        that flag suspicious transactions for review — often before the cardholder is even aware their account has been
        compromised.</p>
