      <h3>5.3 Threat Intelligence Visualisation</h3>
      <p>Threat intelligence involves understanding the tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) of adversary groups.
        In VR, analysts can explore attack kill-chains as three-dimensional maps — walking through each stage of an
        attack, seeing how one compromised machine connects to another, and understanding the attacker's full lateral
        movement path through the network in a way that a 2D diagram simply cannot convey.</p>

      <h3>5.4 Security Awareness Training for Non-Technical Staff</h3>
      <p>The weakest link in any security system is often the human being. VR makes security awareness training far more
        memorable than a PowerPoint presentation. Employees experience a simulated phishing attack, a fake phone scam,
        or a physical tailgating attempt in VR — the emotional experience of almost falling for it creates lasting
        behavioural change that classroom instruction rarely achieves.</p>
    </section>

