      <h2>8. Advantages &amp; Disadvantages</h2>

      <h3>8.1 AI in Cybersecurity</h3>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros-side">
          <h4>✅ Advantages</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Speed:</strong> Analyses millions of events per second — far beyond human capacity</li>
            <li><strong>24/7 monitoring:</strong> Never tired, never distracted, always vigilant</li>
            <li><strong>Early detection:</strong> Identifies threats days or weeks before human analysts would notice
            </li>
            <li><strong>Reduced false positives:</strong> Advanced models improve in accuracy over time</li>
            <li><strong>Scalability:</strong> Protects 10 devices or 10 million equally well</li>
            <li><strong>Automation:</strong> Responds in milliseconds rather than hours</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cons-side">
          <h4>❌ Disadvantages</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Adversarial AI:</strong> Attackers use AI too — for deepfakes and evasion</li>
            <li><strong>Data dependency:</strong> Biased or incomplete training data causes poor models</li>
            <li><strong>Black-box problem:</strong> Deep learning models are hard to interpret for legal proceedings
            </li>
            <li><strong>High cost:</strong> Implementation and expertise are expensive</li>
            <li><strong>Privacy concerns:</strong> Continuous monitoring raises civil liberties issues</li>
            <li><strong>Overconfidence:</strong> Over-reliance on AI can create blind spots</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>8.2 VR &amp; AR in Cybersecurity</h3>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros-side">
          <h4>✅ Advantages</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Safe practice:</strong> Train for catastrophic attacks with zero real-world risk</li>
            <li><strong>Better retention:</strong> Experiential learning sticks far better than lectures</li>
            <li><strong>Intuitive visualisation:</strong> Complex data becomes understandable in 3D</li>
            <li><strong>Remote collaboration:</strong> Teams work together across geographic distances</li>
            <li><strong>Evidence clarity:</strong> VR reconstructions make digital evidence accessible to juries</li>
            <li><strong>Cost reduction:</strong> Replaces expensive physical training exercises</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cons-side">
          <h4>❌ Disadvantages</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Hardware cost:</strong> Quality headsets and infrastructure are expensive</li>
            <li><strong>Motion sickness:</strong> Some users experience discomfort with extended use</li>
            <li><strong>Simulation gap:</strong> Virtual environments cannot perfectly replicate reality</li>
            <li><strong>Privacy risk:</strong> AR systems processing physical environments collect sensitive data</li>
            <li><strong>Development cost:</strong> Building realistic virtual environments requires major resources</li>
            <li><strong>Legal scrutiny:</strong> VR reconstructions in court face accuracy challenges</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

